# Skeleton

Holds the place of content while it loads, so the layout does not jump when the content arrives. A skeleton has no size of its own. Set its width and height with `style`, or with a class that targets it.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Skeleton } from "#lib/components/ui/skeleton/index.js";
</script>

<div aria-busy="true" aria-label="Loading profile">
	<Skeleton rounded="pill" style="width: 3rem; height: 3rem" />
	<Skeleton style="width: 15.625rem; height: 1rem" />
	<Skeleton style="width: 12.5rem; height: 1rem" />
</div>
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/skeleton.json
```

## Sizing

Inline `style` is the recommended way to size a skeleton. To size skeletons with a class instead, see the other ways on the [styling page](/docs/styling).

## Accessibility

Each skeleton sets `aria-hidden="true"`, so screen readers skip the placeholders. Set `aria-busy="true"` and an `aria-label` on the element that holds them, and remove `aria-busy` when the content loads.

## Card

Combine skeletons to match the shape of the content they replace, such as a card with a title, a description, and an image.

<Demo section="card" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Skeleton } from "#lib/components/ui/skeleton/index.js";
	import { Card, CardHeader, CardContent } from "#lib/components/ui/card/index.js";
</script>

<Card aria-busy="true" aria-label="Loading post" style="width: 20rem">
	<CardHeader>
		<Skeleton style="width: 66%; height: 1rem" />
		<Skeleton style="width: 50%; height: 1rem" />
	</CardHeader>
	<CardContent>
		<Skeleton style="aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; width: 100%" />
	</CardContent>
</Card>
```

## Rounded

Set `rounded` to `xs` through `4xl` or `pill` to override the default `md` radius. Use `pill` for avatars and pills.

<Demo section="rounded" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Skeleton rounded="pill" style="width: 3rem; height: 3rem" />
```

## API

The `Skeleton` props extend the native `div` attributes, and extra attributes pass through to the element. When the user prefers reduced motion, the pulse stops.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface Props extends CompProps<"div"> {
	/** Corner radius; `md` when omitted */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
}
```
